      "side": 1,
      "message": "The additional `addr` argument works. Another problem is that `answer_call()` is a DBus handler so I\u0027d like to block it unless we\u0027re in the MPS mode. How about:\n1. Move as many duplicated code (such as `phone_state_change` / `start_sco_call_impl` / `simple_at_response`) into the `xxxx_impl` functions\n2. Callbacks / DBus handlers simply call the impl functions with / without `addr`\n3. All DBus handlers, `HfpCallbacks::DialCall`, and `HfpCallbacks::CallHold` early return if not in MPS mode\n4. Remove most of the MPS mode check.",
